'''Tuberaceæ''' (tū-bẹ-rā′sẹ̄-ē), ''n. pl.'' [NL., < L. ''tuber'', a tuber, + ''-aceæ''.] An order of hypogenous or subepigenous discomycetous fungi, typified by the genus ''Tuber'', having the gleba traversed by veins, and one- to eight-spored asci.

'''tuberated''' (tū′bẹ-rā-ted), ''a.'' [< LL. ''tuberatus'', covered with knots or bosses (< L. ''tuber'', a knob, boss: see ''tuber''), + ''-ed''<sup>2</sup>.] In ''her.'', having a rounded projection, or more than one. A serpent ''tuberated'' is tied in a knot or a close coil near the middle of the body.
[[FIGURE]]
{{c|{{smaller|Serpent Tuberated.}}}}

